<!-- Application Structure Plan: The SPA is designed around an engineering procurement and system integration workflow rather than a linear document layout. It consists of: 1) Executive Summary & Optimal Procurement Pathways (highlighting the "Modular Body + Lens" conclusion vs. the ELP all-in-one caveat), 2) Interactive System Configurator & FOV Simulator (allowing engineers to pair specific camera bodies and 12mm lenses, calculating real-time FOV, target width at custom distances, estimated BOM cost, and flagging IR-cut/housing/NDAA warnings), 3) Comparative Hardware Explorer (filterable/sortable tables for USB Global Shutter Cameras and 12mm M12 Lenses with direct purchase URLs), 4) Optical & Bandwidth Performance Analytics (Chart.js visualizations comparing sensor FOV coverage and USB 2.0 vs. 3.0 uncompressed vs. MJPEG frame rate bottlenecks), and 5) Pre-Deployment Engineering Checklist (interactive verification cards for IR-cut filters, holder height/enclosure clearance, NDAA Section 889 compliance, and hardware GPIO triggers). This task-oriented structure empowers rapid hardware selection and prevents costly procurement mismatches. -->
<!-- Visualization & Content Choices: 1) Sensor FOV & Coverage Comparison -> Goal: Compare -> Grouped Bar Chart (Chart.js Canvas) comparing HFOV, VFOV, DFOV, and 10m/15m target widths across AR0234CS, IMX392, and OV2311/2312 -> Interaction: Hover tooltips & toggle between degrees and meters -> Justification: Visually clarifies how identical 12mm focal length yields different capture widths depending on optical format. 2) USB Bandwidth & FPS Bottleneck -> Goal: Compare/Analyze -> Horizontal Bar Chart (Chart.js Canvas) comparing theoretical/actual FPS across USB 2.0 vs. USB 3.0 for Uncompressed UYVY/YUY2 vs. MJPEG -> Interaction: Format filter buttons -> Justification: Highlights why USB 2.0 (ELP) forces lossy MJPEG compression while USB 3.0 supports high-speed uncompressed streams. 3) Interactive FOV & BOM Configurator -> Goal: Organize/Synthesize -> Dynamic HTML/CSS/Canvas visual field-of-view cone + live compatibility engine -> Interaction: Dropdown selectors for Camera, Lens, and Target Distance slider -> Justification: Directly solves the report's core challenge of matching separate camera bodies and M12 lenses safely. -->
